From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] arm64: dts: qcom: msm8998: Wire interconnect paths for
 UFS, USB and MDSS

Give the three bandwidth-critical DMA masters whose drivers already
consume interconnect paths their DT wiring: UFS ("ufs-ddr"/"cpu-ufs"),
the USB3 controller ("usb-ddr"/"apps-usb") and the display subsystem
("mdp0-mem"/"cpu-cfg").

This matters because the interconnect driver scales the previously
pinned INT_MAX bus-clock votes down at sync_state: without consumer
votes, storage, USB and display scanout would be left behind a
19.2 MHz keep-alive floor.  With these paths the respective drivers
vote for real bandwidth again.

Other DMA masters (SDCC2, BLSP DMA) have no interconnect support in
their drivers yet; they keep working through the RPM-side aggregation
and the keep-alive floor, and can be wired up when their drivers learn
to vote.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998.dtsi
@@ -8,6 +8,8 @@
 #include <dt-bindings/clock/qcom,mmcc-msm8998.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/clock/qcom,rpmcc.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/firmware/qcom,scm.h>
+#include <dt-bindings/interconnect/qcom,msm8998.h>
+#include <dt-bindings/interconnect/qcom,rpm-icc.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/power/qcom-rpmpd.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/soc/qcom,apr.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/thermal/thermal.h>
@@ -1784,6 +1786,11 @@
 			phy-names = "ufsphy";
 			lanes-per-direction = <2>;
 			power-domains = <&gcc UFS_GDSC>;
+			interconnects = <&a1noc MASTER_UFS RPM_ALWAYS_TAG
+					 &bimc SLAVE_EBI RPM_ALWAYS_TAG>,
+					<&gnoc MASTER_APPS_PROC RPM_ALWAYS_TAG
+					 &cnoc SLAVE_UFS_CFG RPM_ALWAYS_TAG>;
+			interconnect-names = "ufs-ddr", "cpu-ufs";
 			status = "disabled";
 			#reset-cells = <1>;
 
@@ -3102,6 +3109,12 @@
 
 			power-domains = <&gcc USB_30_GDSC>;
 
+			interconnects = <&a1noc MASTER_USB3 RPM_ALWAYS_TAG
+					 &bimc SLAVE_EBI RPM_ALWAYS_TAG>,
+					<&gnoc MASTER_APPS_PROC RPM_ALWAYS_TAG
+					 &cnoc SLAVE_USB3_0 RPM_ALWAYS_TAG>;
+			interconnect-names = "usb-ddr", "apps-usb";
+
 			resets = <&gcc GCC_USB_30_BCR>;
 
 			usb3_dwc3: usb@a800000 {
@@ -3730,6 +3743,12 @@
 			power-domains = <&mmcc MDSS_GDSC>;
 			iommus = <&mmss_smmu 0>;
 
+			interconnects = <&mnoc MASTER_MDP_P0 RPM_ALWAYS_TAG
+					 &bimc SLAVE_EBI RPM_ALWAYS_TAG>,
+					<&gnoc MASTER_APPS_PROC RPM_ALWAYS_TAG
+					 &mnoc SLAVE_DISPLAY_CFG RPM_ALWAYS_TAG>;
+			interconnect-names = "mdp0-mem", "cpu-cfg";
+
 			#address-cells = <1>;
 			#size-cells = <1>;
 			ranges;
